INSERT INTO public.sentences (text, text_zh, notebook_id) VALUES 
('Unless we manipulate our surroundings, we have as little control over what and whom we think about as we do over the muscles of our hearts.', '除非我们操控周围环境，否则我们对自己想什么、想谁的控制力，就像对心肌的控制力一样微弱。', 31),
('Corollary to Moore''s Law: every ten years, collective wisdom degrades by half.', '摩尔定律的推论：每十年，集体智慧就会衰减一半。', 31),
('Never rid anyone of an illusion unless you can replace it in his mind with another illusion. (But don''t work too hard on it; the replacement illusion does not even have to be more convincing than the initial one.)', '永远不要消除任何人的幻觉，除非你能在他心中用另一个幻觉来替代。（但不要太费力；替代的幻觉甚至不必比最初的更有说服力。）', 31),
('The tragedy is that much of what you think is random is in your control and, what''s worse, the opposite.', '悲剧在于，你认为随机的很多事情实际上在你的控制之下，更糟糕的是，情况往往相反。', 31),
('The fool views himself as more unique and others more generic; the wise views himself as more generic and others more unique.', '愚者视自己为独特，他人为平庸；智者视自己为平庸，他人为独特。', 31),
('What made medicine fool people for so long was that its successes were prominently displayed and its mistakes (literally) buried.', '医学之所以能长期愚弄人们，是因为它的成功被显著展示，而错误则被（字面意思上）埋葬了。', 31),
('The sucker''s trap is when you focus on what you know and what others don''t know, rather than the reverse.', '傻瓜陷阱就是专注于你知道而别人不知道的事情，而不是相反。', 31),
('Medieval man was a cog in a wheel he did not understand; modern man is a cog in a complicated system he thinks he understands.', '中世纪的人是他不理解的轮子中的齿轮；现代人是他自以为理解的复杂系统中的齿轮。', 31),
('The calamity of the information age is that the toxicity of data increases much faster than its benefits.', '信息时代的灾难在于，数据的毒性增长速度远超其益处。', 31),
('The role of the media is best seen in the journey from Cato the Elder to a modern politician. Do some extrapolation if you want to be scared.', '媒体的作用最好通过从老加图到现代政治家的历程来理解。如果你想被吓到，可以做些推断。', 31),
('Mental clarity is the child of courage, not the other way around.', '心智清晰是勇气的产物，而非相反。', 31),
